                <pb facs="0421" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.852/71</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10018</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-14">February 14, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received February
                        19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to record below a report
                    made to me by the Commercial Attaché relative to the proposed purchase of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Tine Asmussen</hi>: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I asked Professor Silva Herzog, Manager of Distribuidora de Petroleos
                            Mexicanos, on February 14th, if he had purchased the German tanker, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tine Asmussen</hi> from W. R. Davis. He said
                            that the matter stood just where it had been for some time and,
                            consequently, the vessel had not been purchased. He said that the price
                            placed on the tanker by W. R. Davis was 350,000.00 dollars of which
                            50,000.00 dollars would be paid in cash and the remainder in petroleum
                            products.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
